      "conf": "VERIFIED · PRIMARY + VENDOR",
      "dek": "American share futures are almost exactly where they closed: the S&P 500 contract is 7,763.00, down 0.05%, after Thursday's flat finish at 7,704.13. Overnight the world pulled in two directions. Japan's Nikkei 225 rose 1.18% to 66,286.04, carried by the firms that build chip-making machines, while Hong Kong's Hang Seng fell 1.58% to 24,370.72 and oil dropped 2.02% to $92.70, handing back Thursday's jump. Nothing in that tips the US either way, and that is the point: long-term borrowing costs repriced three days running this week, and share prices still have not argued with it. August factory orders land at 13:30 UK.",
