      "conf": "VERIFIED · PRIMARY FILING",
      "dek": "A Form 4 reached the SEC at 21:33 UK on Thursday, 33 minutes after the closing bell. Vlad Tenev, Robinhood's chief executive, converted 240,834 shares on 22 September and sold every one, at $125.33 and $126.14 - about $30.2m, and roughly 3.7% above Thursday's $120.82 close. His direct holding of those shares is now zero, which sounds worse than it is: he still holds 47,794,572 of the other share class, so the sale was 0.50% of his stake, made under a pre-set plan he adopted on 5 September 2025. For a long-term holder that is a calendar, not a verdict. The shares are $121.51 overnight.",
