      "dek": "Micron traded $1,087.64 in the overnight session, 0.66% above Thursday's $1,080.53 close and $6.60 above the highest price it reached during Thursday's trading - a new high set while New York was shut. The same part of the chain led Japan: Tokyo Electron rose 4.08% and Advantest 2.36%, the two firms that sell the machines memory factories buy. That matters because memory is the piece of the AI build-out with real pricing power at the moment. Micron's fourth-quarter results are expected on 30 September, a date I still cannot confirm at a primary source. Nvidia is $224.75 overnight.",
