      "conf": "VERIFIED · PRIMARY FILING INDEX",
      "dek": "I re-read Oracle's filing record at the SEC this morning with a fresh request, because an absence is exactly the claim a stale copy fakes. The newest document is still dated 23 SEP, six of them accepted between 23:06 and 23:22 UTC, and there is no entry for 24 September. That is two full sessions in which the company has disclosed nothing, after the report that knocked its shares and pulled the private-credit lender Blue Owl down with it. Oracle closed 3.47% lower at $139.54 and Blue Owl 3.65% lower at $9.25, a gap of 0.18 percentage points. Watch for an 8-K from either side.",
