      "dek": "Today's one scheduled American release is the advance report on orders for long-lasting manufactured goods - machinery, aircraft, computers, the things companies buy when they are confident. The Census Bureau's own schedule puts the August report at 8:30 a.m. New York time, 13:30 UK, and its report page still carries July, so it genuinely has not published yet. July's orders were $339.3bn, up 1.1%. The line to watch is business spending on equipment, because that is where the money going into data centres and AI hardware eventually shows up in the national figures. The fuller August report follows on 2 October.",
